<title>TURKEY: Turk Netas signs $24 mln Telekom deal.</title>
<headline>Turk Netas signs $24 mln Telekom deal.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish telecommunications equipment producer Netas- Northern Electric Telekomunikasyon A.S. signed a $24 million agreement with the state-owned Turk Telekom, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Netas, owned 51.85 percent by Canada's Northern Telecom, will undertake the second phase of a project for remote maintenance and management of Turk Telekom switches in rural areas.</p>
<p>Netas had also won the first phase of the project in 1994.</p>
<p>The project will increase revenues and efficiency and cut maintenance expenses of Turk Telekom, the centrepiece of Turkey's privatisation programme.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 0875. SY EKS</p>
